Z||000002||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||08:14 AM||||they will work but you'll have to either remove the trunk lock or still pull the pins and then unlock the hatch... they will have to mount through the taillight housing just make sure you use a set of bracing washers cause the nuts supplied tend to pull through even metal frames if they aren't' braced properly... (i ate a customers hood at 30mph... the wind caught it.. ripped it up and smashed the windshield, the sunroof and scare the CRAP out of me) I realize that the wind shouldn't catch the rear hatch but the vibrations will chew the Fiberglas away and cause the pins to fail. IF they aren't braced properly <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||04-03-2001||03:15 PM||||why not try the ones that mount flush, has a key to open them, then you can do away with the factory lock. I been thinking of them myself.||||reg||1
